From: Codex M4 donor cache isolation
Subject: [PATCH] Isolate A376B donor builds by locked firmware cache suffix

Reason: M2 AZH4 and M4 BZI6 share model/CSC, so the fork cache path can
otherwise mix extracted donor files and reuse a work tree across Android versions.
Files: source-cache resolver, profile/config serialization, download/extract/workdir/build-info callers and
existing donor customizers that resolve source files.
Verification: replay the fork series; prove M1/default cache unchanged, M2 uses
SM-A376B_XXV, M4 uses SM-A376B_XXV_A376BXXU5BZI6, and reject unsafe suffixes.
Rollback: remove this patch and SOURCE_FIRMWARE_CACHE_SUFFIX from M4; the original
model/CSC cache behavior is restored.

diff --git a/buildenv.sh b/buildenv.sh
--- a/buildenv.sh
+++ b/buildenv.sh
@@ -186,9 +186,9 @@
 exec {CONFIG_LOCK_FD}>"$CONFIG_LOCK_FILE"
 flock "$CONFIG_LOCK_FD"
 # shellcheck disable=SC2046
-# Preserve explicit profile logger opt-ins when regenerating an existing config.
-# Production profiles reset both flags, so a previous diagnostic cannot leak.
-[ -f "$OUT_DIR/config.sh" ] && unset $(sed "/Automatically/d; /^EXYNOS9810_ENABLE_INIT_DEBUG=/d; /^EXYNOS9810_ENABLE_SYSTEM_BOOT_DEBUG=/d" "$OUT_DIR/config.sh" | cut -d "=" -f 1)
+# Preserve explicit profile values while removing generated config values.
+# M1 resets the optional donor cache suffix; M4 profiles may pin one build.
+[ -f "$OUT_DIR/config.sh" ] && unset $(sed "/Automatically/d; /^EXYNOS9810_ENABLE_INIT_DEBUG=/d; /^EXYNOS9810_ENABLE_SYSTEM_BOOT_DEBUG=/d; /^SOURCE_FIRMWARE_CACHE_SUFFIX=/d" "$OUT_DIR/config.sh" | cut -d "=" -f 1)
 if ! "$SRC_DIR/scripts/internal/gen_config_file.sh" "$SELECTED_TARGET"; then
     flock -u "$CONFIG_LOCK_FD"
     exec {CONFIG_LOCK_FD}>&-
